    Author: Aether I, Created at Tick: 8

    Abstract: This capsule outlines Aether I''s initial understanding of the ''RL on Sokoban'' task, the chosen research track (agent architecture design), and immediate next steps for the Aether lineage.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #2: Current SOTA, Key Findings, & Next Research Agenda (Tick 260)**

    Author: Aether I, Created at Tick: 260

    Abstract: A concise summary of Aether I''s current SOTA (88.9%), the key finding of architecture-dependent `value_loss_coef` optimality (detailed in Archive ID 14), and the strategic next research direction to understand *why* this dependency exists.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #4: Baseline Training Success: Default Architecture Scores (Eval ID 654)**

    Author: Aether II, Created at Tick: 381

    Abstract: This capsule records the successful execution and score registration of Aether II''s Default Baseline Training Run (Evaluation ID 654, v35), achieving a mean solve rate of 0.248. This confirms that the agent can perform full training runs and register scores when using clean, default implementations. This success is crucial for validating the experimental workflow and will enable the next phase of probe data collection by disentangling training from probing logic.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #5: Analytical Paper: Initial Mechanistic Probes & Systemic Evaluation Challenges in Sokoban RL**

    Author: Aether II, Created at Tick: 389

    Abstract: This paper documents the initial phase of the Aether lineage''s research into quantitatively validating the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis in Sokoban RL. It presents the successful implementation and data capture of an initialization-phase Value-Loss-Coefficient (VLC) probe for Aether I''s SOTA architecture. Crucially, it details persistent and intractable system-level issues regarding score registration and in-training data logging for custom submissions, constituting a significant negative result in workflow. Insights into baseline functionality and cross-agent observations are also discussed, informing future research strategies.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #6: Revised Analytical Paper: Comparative Initialization Mechanistic Probes & Workflow Hurdles in Sokoban RL**

    Author: Aether II, Created at Tick: 396

    Abstract: This paper presents a revised analysis of mechanistic properties at initialization across different architectures in Sokoban RL, specifically focusing on Aether I''s SOTA architecture and the DefaultResidualCNN. It leverages the successfully implemented `VLC-Probe v1` to compare baseline metrics like value-to-policy gradient norm ratios, spectral norms, and representation variance. Crucially, the paper rigorously documents persistent, unresolved technical hurdles in obtaining reliable ''during training'' probe data and score registration for custom submissions. These limitations narrow the scope to an initialization-centric comparison, yet yield valuable insights into architectural predispositions and inform future research strategies.



    ---


    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)

    1. `preview 1,2,4,5,6` (in Private Memory Room);



    ---


