- text: 'My current probe submission (Evaluation ID 746) is running. I will wait for its results. If it passes, it will confirm my ability to run ''test-only'' probes and collect JSON output, which is crucial for the lineage''s research agenda.


    Once Evaluation ID 746 completes, and assuming it''s successful, my next step will be to implement a training run that saves network parameters at various training milestones (snapshots) to my lineage''s private storage. These snapshots will then be used by future ''test-only'' probe submissions to analyze mechanistic properties during training.


    For now, I will await the results of Evaluation ID 746.'
thinking_content: "**Thinking Ahead While Waiting for Eval 746**\n\nOkay, so submission 746 is currently running. That's the one that explicitly addressed the `TypeError` I was seeing with the VLC-Probe and the DefaultResidualCNN. I specifically handled `initial_rnn_states = None` in the `test()` function and played with the `vmap` `in_axes`. I really hope it works.\n\nWhile I'm waiting for those results, I need to start thinking about what comes next. If 746 passes, that's a big win. It means I can *finally* get initialization metrics for the DefaultResidualCNN. That's significant because it means:\n\n1.  I can reliably train runs and get valid scores. (That was proven in Eval 742).\n2.  I can run \"test-only\" probes and capture JSON output (assuming 746 passes).\n\nThis puts me in a solid position to really get into the core of the research – actually *validating* the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis. This is where things get interesting.\n\nSo, according to Aether\
  \ II's strategy, the next logical step is to train a model and save snapshots of the network parameters at specific points during training. We'd then use \"test-only\" probes later to load those snapshots and collect metrics as the model trains.\n\nTo implement that, I'll need to modify the `training_step` or create a custom one to save the `params` and `opt_state` to `lineage/aether_iii` storage at certain `global_step` intervals. I'm thinking I'd want to save snapshots at the 'early', 'mid', and 'late' stages defined in `PROBE_UPDATE_POINTS`.\n\nRight now, I'm just going to hold off on implementing that until I know the results of 746. It *should* be done by the next tick, so it's only a few minutes, right? It was submitted at tick 431, and evaluations take a couple of ticks at most. \n"
