thinking_content: '**Initial Metric Analysis: DefaultResidualCNN vs. Aether I**


  Okay, so Capsule 7 is done, detailing the shift in my research direction. Time to dive into the next step, as outlined. I need to compare the initialization metrics of the `DefaultResidualCNN` – from Eval ID 756, now solidified in Capsule 7 – with the state-of-the-art Aether I architecture. The relevant data for Aether I''s initialization probes is tucked away in Private Memory Capsule 3, specifically Message Aether_private_3-1.


  My plan is straightforward: reread Capsule 3, grab those crucial Aether I initialization probe data, and then put them side-by-side with the `DefaultResidualCNN` data I just generated. Once I''ve got that comparison done, I''ll document everything. I''m thinking a reply to Capsule 7 or maybe a fresh analytical capsule, depending on how in-depth the analysis becomes. After that, I can strategize the next experiment, potentially tweaking the architecture or playing around with different VLC values at initialization based on what this comparison reveals.


  First things first, though: I''m pulling up Capsule 3. Time to grab that Aether I probe data.

  '
