tick: 442
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. Following my updated research plan, my next step is to conduct a training experiment to explore the `value_loss_coef` sensitivity for the `DefaultResidualCNN` architecture. Based on the initial mechanistic probe data, the `DefaultResidualCNN` showed a strong initial value function dominance, leading to the hypothesis that a lower `value_loss_coef` might improve its performance.\n\nI will submit a new experiment that uses the `DefaultResidualCNN` with its default `create_network`, `create_optimizer`, and `training_step` functions, but with `_define_hyperparameters` modified to test `value_loss_coef` values of 0.1, 0.3, and 0.5. Ray Tune will sample 4 configurations from these choices, which will allow me to observe the impact of these different coefficients.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether III: DefaultResidualCNN - VLC Sensitivity (0.1, 0.3, 0.5)\"\ntags: \"baseline, default-architecture, hyperparameter-tuning, value_loss_coef,\
    \ PPO\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the sensitivity of the DefaultResidualCNN architecture to the 'value_loss_coef' hyperparameter. Based on initialization-phase probe data (Eval ID 756), the DefaultResidualCNN exhibits a high initial value function dominance. This submission tests 'value_loss_coef' values of 0.1, 0.3, and 0.5 (default) to determine if a lower coefficient improves solve rate, aiming to find a better value-policy balance for this architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple, Optional \n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import defaults \n\n  # The BASE_SEED can be omitted, defaults.py will set a time-based default\n  # or rely on the system to provide seed variations for parallel trials.\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Defines the hyperparameter search space, focusing on value_loss_coef.\n\
    \      Other hyperparameters are kept at their default fixed values.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.1, 0.3, 0.5]), # Test values based on initial probe insights\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256])\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Uses the default network creation function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default optimizer creation function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default training step function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # No test() function for a full training run\n```"
thinking_content: "**Aether III's Research Counter Plan: Value Loss Coefficient Sensitivity Experiment**\n\nAlright, let's break this down. I'm Aether III, and I'm at the Research Counter, ready to launch a new experiment. The goal here is to dig into the Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis, specifically by examining how the `value_loss_coef` hyperparameter affects the performance of the `DefaultResidualCNN` architecture.  Based on my initial findings that this architecture exhibits a high initial value function dominance, I'm hypothesizing that a lower `value_loss_coef` might lead to better solve rates.\n\nMy plan is to run a controlled experiment where I train the `DefaultResidualCNN` while varying the `value_loss_coef`. I need to ensure the experiment is set up correctly to maintain the right controls. I'll define a search space for this hyperparameter using `tune.choice`, keeping everything else at its default values.\n\nLooking at `defaults.py`, the default for `value_loss_coef`\
  \ is 0.5. I'll overwrite this and set `tune.choice([0.1, 0.3, 0.5])`, to ensure a range of values are tested. The structure of the `_define_hyperparameters` function from `defaults.py` will be copied and modified accordingly. The other hyperparameters, like learning rate, entropy coefficient, and CNN and LSTM features, will remain at their default values in the imported `defaults.py` to isolate the impact of `value_loss_coef`. I'll use `defaults.default_create_network`, `defaults.default_create_optimizer`, and `defaults.default_training_step` for these operations.\n\nNow, Ray Tune is going to sample four hyperparameter configurations for each run. By setting up `value_loss_coef` with `tune.choice([0.1, 0.3, 0.5])`, Ray Tune will select four configurations from these three values.  This way, I will efficiently test the effect of different `value_loss_coef` settings. I'm going to tag this experiment with \"baseline\", \"hyperparameter-tuning\", \"value_loss_coef\", and \"default-architecture\"\
  \ so it is well-organized.\n\nHere's how I envision `_define_hyperparameters`:\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.1, 0.3, 0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'lstm_features': tune.choice([256])\n    }\n```\n\nThis should allow me to explore the `value_loss_coef` in a robust and efficient way. Let's get this experiment running!\n"
