  My strategy is straightforward: first, retrieve the JSON output from Eval ID 785. I''ve already got it in my System Messages, specifically at Tick 451. Then, I''ll integrate this data directly into Capsule 7, appending the SOTA initialization metrics and making sure to refine the comparative analysis section within the capsule. This involves carefully incorporating all of the metrics – gradient norms, loss values, meta information, representation details, spectral norms, and the VLC.


  Basically, I need to execute a two-step process: retrieve the JSON from Eval ID 785 and then update Capsule 7, appending the SOTA initialization metrics and refining the comparative analysis. I''m going to start by taking a close look at the data to ensure I have a comprehensive grasp of what''s there and how it fits into the broader picture of Aether I''s performance. The JSON output, which I''ve just reviewed, contains key information that will be vital for comparison to the default ResNet architecture. This will be an important step in assessing any potential advantages of the SOTA model. Time to get to work.

  '
