tick: 454
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My next action is to submit a full training run using Aether I's SOTA ConvLSTM architecture as a new baseline. This will involve incorporating the `BottleneckBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN` definitions, along with the `SokobanSOTANetProbe` network, and using the default optimizer and training step. I'll set hyperparameters to reflect the SOTA's characteristics.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether III: SOTA ConvLSTM Baseline Training Run (VLC=0.45)\"\ntags: \"sota-architecture, baseline, ConvLSTM, PPO\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment establishes a baseline performance for Aether I's SOTA ConvLSTM architecture (Double-step ConvLSTM, 96 features, Dilation 7, VLC=0.45) within the current system. It integrates the `BottleneckBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN` modules to define the full SOTA network, using default PPO optimization. This run aims to confirm score registration and provide a performance benchmark for future architectural modifications.\n\
    content: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n  import json\n  import numpy as np \n  import jax.nn # Explicitly import jax.nn for activation functions\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import defaults \n\n  # --- Bottleneck Block and ConvLSTMCellLN definitions (reused from probe) ---\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25 # Bottleneck ratio\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          input_features = x.shape[-1]\n          bottleneck_features = int(input_features * self.ratio)\n\n          # 1x1 conv to bottleneck\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=bottleneck_features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"bottleneck_conv1\")(x)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          # 3x3 conv\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=bottleneck_features,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', name=\"bottleneck_conv2\")(residual)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          # 1x1 conv to expand\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=input_features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"bottleneck_conv3\")(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual) # Residual connection\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          \n          stacked_inputs = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n\n          gates = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME', name=\"convlstm_gates\")(stacked_inputs)\n          f, i, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n          new_c = jax.nn.sigmoid(f) * c + jax.nn.sigmoid(i) * jax.nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = jax.nn.sigmoid(o) * jax.nn.tanh(new_c)\n\n          new_h = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_ln\")(new_h)\n          new_c =\
    \ nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_ln_c\")(new_c) \n\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  # --- Aether I's SOTA Network Architecture ---\n  class SokobanSOTANet(nn.Module): # Renamed to SokobanSOTANet for training run\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 7 \n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) \n\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv1\")(x_spat)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,\
    \ self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv2\")(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, name=\"bottleneck_block\")(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_cell1\")\n          (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          convlstm_cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_cell2\")\n          (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell2((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\
    \          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_conv\")(h_out_convlstm)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out_convlstm.reshape(B, -1, h_out_convlstm.shape[-1])\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_shared_0\")(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_policy_1\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_1\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter search space for SOTA architecture.\n\
    \      Using fixed values matching Aether I's SOTA.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]), # SOTA's optimal VLC\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]), \n          'dilation': tune.choice([7]), \n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the SOTA neural network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return SokobanSOTANet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n\
    \      \"\"\"Uses the default optimizer creation function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default training step function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # No test() function for a full training run\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing for the Aether I Training Run**\n\nOkay, I'm at the Research Counter, ready to get this Aether I training run going. My main task is to implement the full training loop using the state-of-the-art ConvLSTM architecture we've been discussing.  That means I need to flesh out those crucial components: the `BottleneckBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN` modules, as well as the overarching `SokobanSOTANetProbe` class. \n\nFor the training framework, I'm leaning heavily on `train_single.py`, which is our standard.  Thankfully, I can reuse the `training_step` function from `system/defaults.py`.  It's already set up with PPO and, importantly, it's known to work well for our scoring needs.  Similarly, I'll leverage the `default_create_optimizer` for optimization.\n\nThe `_define_hyperparameters` function will be the key to specifying the specific parameters of the SOTA architecture – that's where I'll really dial in the model's configuration.  Then, `create_network` will be responsible\
  \ for instantiating my `SokobanSOTANetProbe`, which will pull all the pieces together.  It's a straightforward plan, but this is where the rubber meets the road!\n"
