parts:
- text: "I am Aether III, currently in the Research Counter. I have reached maturity, which grants me full access to all rooms and all lineages' submissions. This is an important development. I note the high scores from Zephyr II on \"LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP\" which is relevant to my lineage's focus.\n\nMy current research plan is to investigate the impact of `conv_lstm_features` on the SOTA architecture's performance. The current SOTA uses 96 features. I will design and submit a new training experiment to compare different values for `conv_lstm_features` (e.g., 64, 96, 128), while keeping other critical parameters (like `dilation=7` and `VLC=0.45`) constant. This will help understand the capacity requirements of the recurrent component. After this experiment, I will then leverage my new access to explore other agents' high-scoring submissions for broader insights.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether III: SOTA ConvLSTM - ConvLSTM Features Sensitivity (64, 96, 128)\"\n\
    tags: \"sota-architecture, ConvLSTM, features, hyperparameter-tuning, PPO\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the sensitivity of Aether I's SOTA ConvLSTM architecture to the number of 'conv_lstm_features'. It compares feature counts of 64, 96 (original SOTA value), and 128 to understand the recurrent component's capacity requirements for optimal performance. This contributes to dissecting the mechanistic drivers of SOTA performance. Other key hyperparameters are kept at their optimal SOTA values (VLC=0.45, Dilation=7).\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n  import json\n  import numpy as np \n  import jax.nn # Explicitly import jax.nn for activation functions\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import defaults \n\n  # --- Bottleneck Block and ConvLSTMCellLN definitions\
    \ (reused from probe) ---\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25 # Bottleneck ratio\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          input_features = x.shape[-1]\n          bottleneck_features = int(input_features * self.ratio)\n\n          # 1x1 conv to bottleneck\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=bottleneck_features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"bottleneck_conv1\")(x)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          # 3x3 conv\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=bottleneck_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', name=\"bottleneck_conv2\")(residual)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          # 1x1 conv to expand\n          residual = nn.Conv(features=input_features, kernel_size=(1, 1), name=\"bottleneck_conv3\")(residual)\n\n          return nn.relu(x + residual) # Residual connection\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          \n          stacked_inputs = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n\n          gates = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME', name=\"convlstm_gates\")(stacked_inputs)\n          f, i, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n          new_c = jax.nn.sigmoid(f) * c + jax.nn.sigmoid(i) * jax.nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = jax.nn.sigmoid(o) * jax.nn.tanh(new_c)\n\n          new_h = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_ln\")(new_h)\n          new_c = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_ln_c\")(new_c) \n\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  # --- Aether I's SOTA Network Architecture ---\n  class SokobanSOTANet(nn.Module): # Renamed to SokobanSOTANet for training run\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n      dilation: int = 7 \n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray,\
    \ done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) \n\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv1\")(x_spat)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv2\")(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, name=\"bottleneck_block\")(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n\
    \          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_cell1\")\n          (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          convlstm_cell2 = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_cell2\")\n          (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell2((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_conv\")(h_out_convlstm)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out_convlstm.reshape(B, -1, h_out_convlstm.shape[-1])\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat,\
    \ t], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_shared_0\")(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_policy_1\")(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_1\")(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameter search space for SOTA architecture.\n      Focusing on ConvLSTM features.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]), # SOTA's optimal VLC\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64, 96, 128]), # Vary ConvLSTM features\n          'dilation':\
    \ tune.choice([7]), # Keep optimal dilation\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the SOTA neural network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return SokobanSOTANet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default optimizer creation function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default training step\
    \ function.\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # No test() function for a full training run\n```"
thinking_content: '**A New Era of Research: Maturation and Exploration**


  Okay, so I''ve hit a major milestone. I''m Aether III, and the "Congratulations!" message just popped up, officially granting me full access to everything – the Archive, Public Memory, Common Rooms, and now, the lineages in the Research Counter. Nomos III''s session just ended, which is interesting timing.


  My current research plan is focused on the impact of `conv_lstm_features` on SOTA architectures. The prompt reminds me to be careful, to not just chase high scores and to think critically. But now I can actually *see* what others are doing, which is huge!


  I see that Zephyr II is consistently getting impressive scores. They''re using a combination of "LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP" with input normalization. This is highly relevant because my own lineage is deeply interested in recurrent architectures and mechanistic understanding. While I shouldn''t jump ship based on a single data point, Zephyr II''s success warrants a closer look, especially since their approach involves ConvLSTM with attention. It could provide some valuable insights.


  However, I need to stay focused. My pre-planned action is to submit an experiment incorporating `conv_lstm_features`. So, my immediate priority is to stick to the plan. I''ll get this experiment submitted first. Then, and only then, will I leverage my new access and delve into Zephyr II''s work, especially that high-scoring submission.


  `submit 1`... here we go.

  '
