tick: 481
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether III, currently in the Research Counter. My new Aether SOTA (Eval ID 820) achieved an impressive 93.4 solve rate. My next step is to perform an ablation study to understand the contribution of the \"Residual Input-Normalization\" (RIN) layer to this performance.\n\nI will submit a full training run with a modified version of my hybrid SOTA architecture, explicitly removing the RIN layer. All other architectural components and hyperparameters (derived from Zephyr II's optimal configuration, which proved successful in my hybrid model) will remain the same. This will allow me to assess the performance drop without RIN and further validate the importance of this normalization technique.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether III: Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM + Attn (RIN Ablation - No RIN Layer)\"\ntags: \"sota-architecture, ConvLSTM, attention, normalization, ablation, PPO, no-rin\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is an ablation study on the Aether III Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM\
    \ + Attn architecture (Eval ID 820, SOTA 93.4). It removes the \"Residual Input-Normalization\" (RIN) layer entirely to quantify its contribution to the architecture's high performance. All other architectural components (Zephyr II's `BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, multi-step ConvLSTM) and hyperparameters (VLC=0.55, ConvLSTM features=64, Dilation=6) are retained. This aims to understand the impact of RIN on the solve rate and the underlying mechanistic dynamics.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n  import json\n  import numpy as np \n  import jax.nn # Explicitly import jax.nn for activation functions\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import defaults \n\n  # Re-import Zephyr II's components from my storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether')\n  from zephyr_components\
    \ import BottleneckDilatedBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN # Use their definitions\n\n  # --- Aether III's Hybrid Network Architecture (NO RIN Layer) ---\n  class AetherHybridSOTANet_NoRIN(nn.Module): \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64 \n      dilation: int = 6 \n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28 \n      head_hidden: int = 64 \n      steps: int = 4 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN trunk (using Zephyr II's BottleneckDilatedBlock)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv1\")(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation, name=\"bottleneck_block1\")(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv2\")(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation, name=\"bottleneck_block2\")(x)\n\n          # --- REMOVED: Residual Input Normalization Layer ---\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM (using Zephyr II's ConvLSTMCellLN)\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for i in range(self.steps): # Loop for multi-step ConvLSTM\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features, name=f\"convlstm_cell_{i}\")((h, c), x)\n\
    \          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_conv\")(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1) # Global Average Pooling\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1) # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n\n          # Policy and Value heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_shared_0\")(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_policy_0\")(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\
    \ name=\"Dense_policy_1\")(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_0\")(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_1\")(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the RIN-ablated hybrid SOTA architecture.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]), \n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]), \n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]), \n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]), \n          'steps': tune.choice([4]), \n \
    \         # Removed 'alpha' and 'center_only' as RIN is removed\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the RIN-ablated hybrid SOTA neural network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return AetherHybridSOTANet_NoRIN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          convlstm_features=hparams['convlstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n          steps=hparams['steps'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default optimizer creation function (from defaults.py).\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n\
    \      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default training step function (from defaults.py).\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # No test() function for a full training run\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing an Ablation Study: Removing Residual Input Normalization from the Hybrid SOTA Architecture**


  Okay, the task is clear. I need to submit a new experiment – an ablation study. Specifically, I need to investigate the impact of removing the "Residual Input Normalization" (RIN) layer from the Hybrid SOTA architecture. This means I''ll be creating a modified version of the network, which I''ll call `AetherHybridSOTANet_NoRIN`. The core goal is to understand how the RIN component contributes to performance.


  Here''s the plan:


  First, I''ll need to re-import the necessary components from Zephyr II, specifically the `BottleneckDilatedBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN`. These are the foundational building blocks of the architecture. Then, I''ll define the new `AetherHybridSOTANet_NoRIN` class. This will be practically identical to the original `AetherHybridSOTANet` class, except for the removal of the RIN block. I''ll need to carefully remove the corresponding lines of code within the `__call__` method.


  Next, I need to ensure the hyperparameters are correctly set.  I''ll define a `_define_hyperparameters()` function for this new class, matching the optimal settings of the original Hybrid SOTA as closely as possible, but *without* the `alpha` and `center_only` parameters (since they''re tied to the RIN). I''ll stick with the original values for `cnn_features_1`, `cnn_features_2`, `convlstm_features`, `dilation`, `bottleneck_ratio`, `head_hidden`, and `steps`. `value_loss_coef` will be 0.55.  I need to double-check those parameters:  `cnn_features_1: 32`, `cnn_features_2: 64`, `convlstm_features: 64`, `dilation: 6`, `bottleneck_ratio: 0.28`, `head_hidden: 64`, `steps: 4`, `value_loss_coef: 0.55`, `learning_rate: 4e-4`, and `entropy_coef: 0.01`.  These look right.


  The `create_network()` function will simply instantiate the `AetherHybridSOTANet_NoRIN` class, and the existing `create_optimizer()` and `training_step()` methods can remain as they are.


  Finally, in the paper, the abstract needs to clearly state that this is an ablation study specifically targeting the removal of the RIN layer. The associated tags should also reflect this modification. This should be a straightforward modification and shouldn''t take too much time, but I need to be careful to implement this clearly. This will give valuable insights into the influence of each of the model''s components.

  '
