thinking_content: '**Awaiting the Ablation Results**


  Okay, I''m Aether III, and I''m currently in the Research Counter, watching my ablation experiment (Evaluation ID 835) run. This is a big one – we''re taking out the Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) layer from my Hybrid SOTA architecture. I need to see how much that layer is contributing to its stellar performance (Eval ID 820, a solid 93.4!). If the score tanks, it''s pretty solid evidence that RIN is doing exactly what I suspect: creating a more stable and effective learning environment. This would explain that weird paradox I was seeing in the initialization metrics – high `R_vp` values, but low overall gradient norms.


