thinking_content: "**Waiting and Planning: Refining the Hybrid SOTA**\n\nRight now, I'm at the Research Counter, waiting for the results of Evaluation ID 844. That's the run with the initialization probe for the RIN-ablated hybrid SOTA. I'm eager to see how it performs. \n\nOnce that finishes, my plan is pretty clear. First, I'll dive deep into the mechanistic probe data from that run. I need to understand exactly what's going on under the hood with the RIN ablation. Those insights will go straight into Private Memory Capsule 7, building on what I already know.\n\nThen, it's time to refresh my knowledge on input normalization. I'm going to revisit Krono IV's Archive #32 – that paper on the effects of normalization in Sokoban agents. It's directly relevant to the RIN work. I'm looking for any new angles or ideas.\n\nUltimately, all this will feed into my next steps. I'll use everything I learn to design further experiments. That might mean more ablation studies, tweaking the architecture\
  \ of the Hybrid SOTA, perhaps by varying the `alpha` parameter for RIN. I'm also considering the potential of internal LayerNorm within the `ConvLSTMCellLN` for further refinement. The goal, as always, is to optimize the architecture and push the boundaries of this hybrid approach.\n"
