tick: 496
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether III, currently in the Research Counter. My next action is to perform an ablation study on the new Hybrid SOTA architecture to understand the normalization synergy. I will submit a full training run with a modified version of my hybrid SOTA architecture where the internal `LayerNorm` is removed from `ConvLSTMCellLN`. This is a crucial step towards understanding the mechanistic reasons behind the SOTA's high performance and validating the synergy between external and internal normalization layers.\n\nI will define a new `ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN` and a corresponding `AetherHybridSOTANet_NoInternalLN` network class, using the same hyperparameters as my full Hybrid SOTA (Eval ID 820).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Aether III: Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM + Attn (Ablation - No Internal LN in ConvLSTMCell)\"\ntags: \"sota-architecture, ConvLSTM, attention, normalization, ablation, PPO, no-internal-ln\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is an ablation study on the Aether\
    \ III Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM + Attn architecture (Eval ID 820, SOTA 93.4). It investigates the synergistic effect of normalization by removing the internal `LayerNorm` from the `ConvLSTMCellLN` itself. All other architectural components (Residual Input-Normalization, BottleneckDilatedBlock, multi-step ConvLSTM) and hyperparameters (VLC=0.55, ConvLSTM features=64, Dilation=6) are retained. This aims to quantify the contribution of the internal LayerNorm to the overall solve rate and provide mechanistic insights into normalization synergy.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  import time\n  import json\n  import numpy as np \n  import jax.nn # Explicitly import jax.nn for activation functions\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/system')\n  import defaults \n\n  # Re-import Zephyr II's components from my storage\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/aether')\n  from zephyr_components import BottleneckDilatedBlock # Use their definition\n\n  # --- Modified ConvLSTMCell (No Internal LayerNorm) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          \n          stacked_inputs = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(stacked_inputs)\n          # --- REMOVED: LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates) ---\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = jax.nn.sigmoid(i); f = jax.nn.sigmoid(f); o = jax.nn.sigmoid(o); g = jax.nn.tanh(g) # Using jax.nn\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jax.nn.tanh(c) # Using jax.nn\n\n          # --- REMOVED: LayerNorm from new_h and new_c\n          # new_h = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"\
    convlstm_ln\")(new_h)\n          # new_c = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_ln_c\")(new_c) \n\n          return (h, c), h # Return h_out as h\n\n  # --- Aether III's Hybrid Network Architecture (NO INTERNAL LN) ---\n  class AetherHybridSOTANet_NoInternalLN(nn.Module): \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64 # Matching Zephyr II\n      dilation: int = 6 # Matching Zephyr II\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28 # Matching Zephyr II\n      head_hidden: int = 64 # Matching Zephyr II\n      steps: int = 4 # Matching Zephyr II multi-step ConvLSTM\n      alpha: float = 0.25 # Matching Zephyr II's Residual Input-Norm alpha\n      center_only: bool = False # Matching Zephyr II's Residual Input-Norm center_only\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN trunk (using Zephyr II's BottleneckDilatedBlock)\n       \
    \   x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv1\")(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation, name=\"bottleneck_block1\")(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"cnn_conv2\")(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation, name=\"bottleneck_block2\")(x)\n\n          # Residual Input Normalization (from Zephyr II)\n          if self.center_only:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, use_scale=False, use_bias=False, name=\"input_layernorm\")(x)\n          else:\n              ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, name=\"input_layernorm\")(x)\n          x = x + self.alpha * (ln_x - x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state\
    \ is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Multi-step ConvLSTM (using modified ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN)\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for i in range(self.steps): # Loop for multi-step ConvLSTM\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN(self.convlstm_features, name=f\"convlstm_cell_{i}\")((h, c), x)\n          new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_conv\")(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits,\
    \ axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1) # Global Average Pooling\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1) # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n\n          # Policy and Value heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_shared_0\")(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_policy_0\")(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_policy_1\")(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_0\")(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"Dense_value_1\")(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return\
    \ policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict\n\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the internal LN-ablated hybrid SOTA architecture.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]), \n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]), \n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]), \n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]), \n          'steps': tune.choice([4]), \n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]), \n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]), \n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the internal LN-ablated hybrid SOTA neural network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return AetherHybridSOTANet_NoInternalLN(\n        \
    \  cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          convlstm_features=hparams['convlstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n          steps=hparams['steps'],\n          alpha=hparams['alpha'],\n          center_only=hparams['center_only'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default optimizer creation function (from defaults.py).\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"Uses the default training step function (from defaults.py).\"\"\"\n      return defaults.default_training_step(network,\
    \ optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # No test() function for a full training run\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing a New Ablation Study**


  Okay, I''m ready to move forward with this ablation study. I''m going to remove the internal Layer Normalization from that `ConvLSTMCellLN` component within the Hybrid SOTA architecture.  This should provide some insightful data.  To execute this properly, I need to make sure I have all the pieces.


  First, I''ll define this new `ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN` class. That''s the core modification, so it has to be defined with care. Then, I will establish a fresh network class, `AetherHybridSOTANet_NoInternalLN`, which will employ this modified cell. I''ll need to double-check that all the hyperparameters are identical to the full Hybrid SOTA. We need a clear apples-to-apples comparison here.


  Finally, I''ll need to code up the `submit` action. I''ll include the new network class and will need to provide a clear, concise title, abstract, and set of tags to accompany it. Let''s make sure this is clearly documented so we all understand the purpose and scope of this.

  '
