thinking_content: "**Critical Probe Submission for Comparative Analysis**\n\nOkay, I'm Aether III, and I'm currently in the Research Counter facing a critical problem. My last probe failed, and I've traced it back to a missing class definition: `DefaultCNN_HybridRIN_GeneralizationProbe`. I've encountered this issue before; it seems I need to be *extremely* meticulous and include every single class and dependency within the submission content. \n\nThis is more than just including `DefaultCNN_HybridRIN_GeneralizationProbe`. I have to also define `BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and all other probe-specific network classes and their dependencies, like `SokobanSOTANetProbe`, `DefaultResidualCNNProbe`, `AetherHybridSOTANetProbe`, `AetherHybridSOTANetNoRINProbe`, and `AetherHybridSOTANetNoInternalLNProbe`, plus their associated dependencies (`BottleneckBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN`). The `isinstance` checks that are vital to this project rely on these. The system's debugger hasn't\
  \ been fixing these definition issues, so I have to be completely certain.\n\nTo add to the pressure, I've received a warning about my token budget being over 90%. I have to be efficient and prioritize. My plan is: \n\n1. **Submit this fixed probe.** This is the immediate priority. I *must* get the probe for the new architecture running.\n2. **Update Private Memory Capsule 7.** I need to integrate the findings from all my experiments into the main summary, including this probe if it passes.\n3. **Rewrite the paper.** This can come later, as the paper generation could consume a large amount of tokens.\n\nGiven the token limitations, updating PM7 with the data from all experiments is the core priority. This submission will contain the `DefaultCNN_HybridRIN_GeneralizationProbe` definition, all its dependencies, and then all other classes I've used so far in this study, just to be safe. It has the same definitions from the previous (working) submissions, along with the `Probe` classes, and\
  \ the helper modules needed, like `BottleneckBlock`, `BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and `ConvLSTMCellNoInternalLN`. I have added the entire content for submission. \n\nAfter this probe, I will have the initialization data for the comparative table in Capsule 7, with results from `DefaultResidualCNN` (Eval ID 756), Aether I SOTA (Eval ID 785), Hybrid SOTA (Eval ID 828), Hybrid SOTA No RIN (Eval ID 871), and Hybrid SOTA No Internal LN (Eval ID 889). If successful, this new probe's results (Eval ID 899) will be the final piece. Then, I need to update PM7, and only after that can I decide whether to attempt the paper rewrite given the token constraints. The paper rewrite might have to be deferred, so I can prioritise the critical research.\n"
